; Bona — timer for bona-fb-publish.service.
;
; Every 15 minutes from 17:00 to 23:45 Asia/Riyadh, the same window as the Instagram
; publisher. The zone is written INTO the calendar expression, so the schedule holds even if
; this machine's zone changes. Check the next elapse with
;   systemd-analyze calendar "*-*-* 17..23:00/15 Asia/Riyadh"
;
; Why that window: the queue puts every Facebook slot at 20:20 KSA (the evening peak the queue
; generator documents), and the service's --grace 3 h means a tick missed for any reason is
; caught by a later one the same evening. Grace never outlives the window: 20:20 + 3 h lapses
; at 23:20, before the last tick at 23:45, so Persistent=true (run once at the next boot if the
; box was off) cannot post anything the next morning.

[Unit]
Description=Bona — Facebook publisher, every 15 min 17:00–23:59 KSA

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 17..23:00/15 Asia/Riyadh
Persistent=true
AccuracySec=30s
Unit=bona-fb-publish.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
